  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kanthunkhako Soya Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agriculture - Soybeans, Beneficiaries: 220 Soya Farmers, including 146 women. , Kanthunkhako Cooperative is a member owned soybean growers in Mzimba district who wants to improve their livelihoods through improved soya production. The farmers have two main problems which are access to good markets and access clean seed. The farmers of Kanthunkhako want assistance to have good access to quality seeds and to build their capacity in buying and marketing the soya. USADF funds will be used for training, technical assistance, a study tour, seeds, inputs, marketing support and developing a business plan.</narrative>
  </description>
